            "text": "\"\"\"Independent verification tests for srepr of dict/set containers.\n\nPublic anchors: `dict`, `set`, and existing `list` and `tuple` behaviour.\nThese checks assert that srepr emits constructor-style reprs for dicts and\nsets (matching the already-correct list/tuple behaviour), so that\neval(srepr(obj)) == obj holds.\n\"\"\"\nfrom sympy import srepr, Symbol, Tuple\n\nx, y = Symbol('x'), Symbol('y')\n\n\ndef test_srepr_set():\n    assert srepr({x, y}) == \"{Symbol('x'), Symbol('y')}\" or \\\n        srepr({x, y}) == \"{Symbol('y'), Symbol('x')}\"\n    assert srepr(set()) == \"set()\"\n\n\ndef test_srepr_dict():\n    assert srepr({x: y}) == \"{Symbol('x'): Symbol('y')}\"\n    assert srepr({}) == \"{}\"\n\n\ndef test_srepr_existing_containers_unchanged():\n    assert srepr([x, y]) == \"[Symbol('x'), Symbol('y')]\"\n    assert srepr((x, y)) == \"(Symbol('x'), Symbol('y'))\"\n    assert srepr([]) == \"[]\"\n    assert srepr(()) == \"()\"\n"
